# Merciful Mandate ({1}{W}) ends the combat phase: the game skips straight to the postcombat main phase, and the end of
# combat step is skipped, so "at end of combat" abilities don't trigger (CR 724.2d-e). Kytheon, Hero of Akros and two
# Ornithopters attack on turn three, which would transform Kytheon at end of combat (his own scenarios show it); Bot1 casts
# the Mandate in the declare attackers step and ends the phase. No damage is dealt, Kytheon stays Kytheon, and the
# attackers are untapped by the spell's first sentence. The spell is exiled (724.2b).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Kytheon, Hero of Akros
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Merciful Mandate
Plains
Plains
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Kytheon, Hero of Akros.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Attack(Kytheon, Hero of Akros > Bot2; Ornithopter#1 > Bot2; Ornithopter#2 > Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Merciful Mandate.Cast
Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Step = Main2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Kytheon, Hero of Akros.Tapped = false

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield = Kytheon, Hero of Akros; Ornithopter; Ornithopter; Plains; Plains
Bot1.Exile.Merciful Mandate.Colors.Count = 1
